      "writtenOn": "2025-01-29T00:36:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, so, the motivation of these changes is paying for the 16 KB w/o sparsity changes (a small market segment, due to the issue in b/376814207). If these changes get in, then users get that, users fill up space, then the changes adding 16 KB w/o sparsity would be a real size increase on those devices, causing us not to be able to merge it.\n\nSo, we need to make sure all 4 changes happen in a release atomically, and the easiest way to do that is one at a time. If we wait until after the next merge deadline, we could start merging them one at a time. Though, being able to do it at once (and revert together) even if it is more errorprone or makes it more likely for a full topic revert is a bit easier than tracking branches/dates/etc..",
